docs: assets caught up, and say plainly what has not been checked

The asset section was rewritten yesterday when the mappers first became
readable. Since then the feature grew a good deal — completion inside
`n:asset`, a popup that opens on its own and again after a mapper's colon,
navigation from the mapper prefix to its directory, renaming that leaves a
working template, and reports for the two spellings Latte refuses, each
with a quick fix.

Half the right-hand column now reads "not measured", and that is the
honest state rather than an omission. Those rows cover behaviour added in
the last day; nobody has sat down with the competitor to check them. They
are listed because they are part of what Latte+ does, not as a claim about
what anything else does not.

One row still runs the other way — a path that lands on a directory
instead of a file passes as valid — and the assets root is a convention
with a settings override rather than a setting of its own. Both stay in
"what is still open", where they can be found without reading the table
twice.
